course: dictionary
lesson: 6615
title: Northern: the north part of a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Northern is an adjective. It tells you where something is, or which way it faces. The northern part of a place is the part nearest the north. «France is in the northern half of the world, so July is summer and Christmas is in winter there.» Here northern tells you which half of the world France is in.
explain: Look at the words around northern to work out its meaning. In «Northern Ireland», the word tells you which part of Ireland is meant. In «northern lights», the word tells you where the lights are seen: in the north. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the north part of the world" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Northern can also change form, like other adjectives: more northern and most northern compare places. Northern places on the globe are usually colder, so a more northern place is often colder than one further south.
fact: Northern means in or from the north part of a place.
fact: Northern also means facing or going towards the north.
fact: The Northern Hemisphere is the half of the Earth north of the equator.
fact: The USA, Canada, the UK and Ireland are in the Northern Hemisphere; Australia and New Zealand are in the Southern Hemisphere.
fact: Seasons are opposite in the two halves, so when it is summer in the north, it is winter in the south.
exercise: «Mammoths roamed widely across the northern half of the world.» What does northern mean here? | Very large and hairy | *The north part of the world | Dug up from the ground | Facing the south
exercise: France is in the Northern Hemisphere. What season is it in Australia when it is summer in France? | Spring | Summer, too | *Winter | The same season as in the north
exercise: Which name means the half of the Earth north of the equator? | Northern Ireland | Southern Hemisphere | Northern lights | *Northern Hemisphere
test: In «from what is now Denmark, northern Germany and the Netherlands», what does northern tell you? | That Germany is cold | *Which part of Germany the Angles came from | That the Angles were sailing | That Denmark is a city
test: Which way does a window facing north look? | Towards the south | *Towards the north | Up into the sky | Down at the ground
exam: Which word in «"Mardy" is Midlands and Northern English slang for sulky» names a region of England? | Slang | Mardy | Sulky | *Northern
